org.nem.nis.controller.NodeController.boot Boots the network. <pre><code>inline void org::nem::nis::controller::NodeController::boot (
    @RequestBody final Deserializer deserializer
) 
</code></pre> <p>Parameters:</p> <ul> <li><code>deserializer</code> Information about the primary node including the private key. </li> </ul>

org.nem.nis.controller.NodeController.canYouSeeMe Just return the Node info the requester "Can You See Me" using the IP address from the request. <pre><code>inline NodeEndpoint org::nem::nis::controller::NodeController::canYouSeeMe (
    @RequestBody final NodeEndpoint localEndpoint,
    final HttpServletRequest request
) 
</code></pre> <p>Parameters:</p> <ul> <li><code>localEndpoint</code> The local endpoint (what the local node knows about itself). </li> <li><code>request</code> The http servlet request. </li> </ul> <p>Returns:</p> <p>The endpoint. </p>

org.nem.nis.controller.NodeController.getActivePeerList Gets a dynamic list of the active nodes to which the running node broadcasts information. <pre><code>inline AuthenticatedResponse &lt; SerializableList &lt; Node &gt; &gt; org::nem::nis::controller::NodeController::getActivePeerList (
    @RequestBody final NodeChallenge challenge
) 
</code></pre> <p>Parameters:</p> <ul> <li><code>challenge</code> The challenge. </li> </ul> <p>Returns:</p> <p>A list of broadcast partners. </p>

org.nem.nis.controller.NodeController.getAuthenticatedExperiences Gets the local node's experiences. <pre><code>inline AuthenticatedResponse &lt; NodeExperiencesPair &gt; org::nem::nis::controller::NodeController::getAuthenticatedExperiences (
    @RequestBody final NodeChallenge challenge
) 
</code></pre> <p>Returns:</p> <p>Information about the experiences the local node has had with other nodes. </p>

org.nem.nis.controller.NodeController.getInfo Gets information about the running node. <pre><code>inline AuthenticatedResponse &lt; Node &gt; org::nem::nis::controller::NodeController::getInfo (
    @RequestBody final NodeChallenge challenge
) 
</code></pre> <p>Parameters:</p> <ul> <li><code>challenge</code> The challenge. </li> </ul> <p>Returns:</p> <p>Information about the running node. </p>

org.nem.nis.controller.NodeController.ping Ping that means the pinging node is part of the NEM P2P network. <pre><code>inline void org::nem::nis::controller::NodeController::ping (
    @RequestBody final NodeExperiencesPair nodeExperiencesPair,
    final HttpServletRequest request
) 
</code></pre> <p>This is only provided for backwards compatibility.</p> <p>Parameters:</p> <ul> <li><code>nodeExperiencesPair</code> Information about the experiences the pinging node has had with other nodes. </li> <li><code>request</code> The http servlet request. </li> </ul>

org.nem.nis.controller.NodeController.signOfLife A node is signalling that it is part of the NEM P2P network. <pre><code>inline void org::nem::nis::controller::NodeController::signOfLife (
    @RequestBody final Node node,
    final HttpServletRequest request
) 
</code></pre> <p>Parameters:</p> <ul> <li><code>node</code> Information about the node. </li> <li><code>request</code> The http servlet request. </li> </ul>

org.nem.nis.controller.PushController.pushBlock Pushes a block to other nodes. <pre><code>inline void org::nem::nis::controller::PushController::pushBlock (
    @RequestBody final Deserializer deserializer
) 
</code></pre> <p>Parameters:</p> <ul> <li><code>deserializer</code> The deserializer that should create a SecureSerializableEntity Block. </li> </ul>

org.nem.nis.controller.PushController.pushTransaction Pushes a transaction to other nodes. <pre><code>inline void org::nem::nis::controller::PushController::pushTransaction (
    @RequestBody final Deserializer deserializer
) 
</code></pre> <p>Parameters:</p> <ul> <li><code>deserializer</code> The deserializer that should create a SecureSerializableEntity Transaction. </li> </ul>

org.nem.nis.controller.PushController.pushTransactions Pushes a list of transactions to other nodes. <pre><code>inline void org::nem::nis::controller::PushController::pushTransactions (
    @RequestBody final Deserializer deserializer,
    HttpServletRequest request
) 
</code></pre> <p>Parameters:</p> <ul> <li><code>deserializer</code> The deserializer that should create a SecureSerializableEntity list of transactions. </li> </ul>

org.nem.nis.controller.TimeSynchronizationController.getNetworkTime Gets the communication time stamps (receive/send network time). <pre><code>inline AuthenticatedResponse &lt; CommunicationTimeStamps &gt; org::nem::nis::controller::TimeSynchronizationController::getNetworkTime (
    @RequestBody final NodeChallenge challenge
) 
</code></pre> <p>Parameters:</p> <ul> <li><code>challenge</code> The challenge. </li> </ul> <p>Returns:</p> <p>The communication time stamps. </p>

org.nem.nis.controller.TransactionController.transactionAnnounce A request for NIS to announce signed transaction data. <pre><code>inline NemAnnounceResult org::nem::nis::controller::TransactionController::transactionAnnounce (
    @RequestBody final RequestAnnounce request
) 
</code></pre> <p>Parameters:</p> <ul> <li><code>request</code> The request, which contains the transaction data and a signature. </li> </ul> <p>Returns:</p> <p>The result of the operation. </p>

org.nem.nis.controller.TransactionController.transactionPrepare A request for NIS to serialize unsigned transaction data into binary for signing by the client. <pre><code>inline RequestPrepare org::nem::nis::controller::TransactionController::transactionPrepare (
    @RequestBody final Deserializer deserializer
) 
</code></pre> <p>This is insecure if an attacker modifies the binary payload in-between NIS and the client.</p> <p>Parameters:</p> <ul> <li><code>deserializer</code> The deserializer that is expected to contain transaction data. </li> </ul> <p>Returns:</p> <p>The binary form of the transaction data. </p>

org.nem.nis.controller.TransactionController.transactionPrepareAnnounce A request for NIS to sign unsigned transaction data and announce it given a private key. <pre><code>inline NemAnnounceResult org::nem::nis::controller::TransactionController::transactionPrepareAnnounce (
    @RequestBody final RequestPrepareAnnounce request
) 
</code></pre> <p>This is insecure if an attacker modifies the binary payload in-between NIS and the client (not to mention it exposes the private key).</p> <p>Parameters:</p> <ul> <li><code>request</code> The request, which contains the transaction data and a private key. </li> </ul> <p>Returns:</p> <p>The result of the operation. </p>

org.nem.nis.controller.TransactionController.transactionsUnconfirmed Gets unconfirmed transaction information. <pre><code>inline AuthenticatedResponse &lt; SerializableList &lt; Transaction &gt; &gt; org::nem::nis::controller::TransactionController::transactionsUnconfirmed (
    @RequestBody final AuthenticatedUnconfirmedTransactionsRequest request
) 
</code></pre> <p>Parameters:</p> <ul> <li><code>request</code> The authenticated unconfirmed transactions request. </li> </ul> <p>Returns:</p> <p>List of unconfirmed transactions. </p>
